WEBVTT

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:22.420
Congratulations.

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:25.800
The enemy has been annihilated four days ahead of schedule.

00:00:26.810 --> 00:00:28.030
We are going back.

00:00:28.030 --> 00:00:30.300
Gather Selvaria and the rest.

00:00:30.300 --> 00:00:30.890
Yes.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:40.940
Did you hear about the mission at Vasel Bridge?

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:44.720
Chapter 4:

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:44.720
Brief Holiday

00:00:40.940 --> 00:00:45.400
I even heard that the guys in the military couldn't do anything.

00:00:45.400 --> 00:00:48.910
Thanks to that victory, the state of affairs is changing.{'state of affairs' lolwtf is this? - 1569}

00:00:48.910 --> 00:00:51.530
The military will have no choice but to pay attention to us.

00:00:52.030 --> 00:00:54.950
Oh, really?

00:00:54.950 --> 00:00:56.370
More importantly...

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:01.010
What's the matter?

00:01:01.010 --> 00:01:02.210
Is something worrying you?

00:01:02.210 --> 00:01:05.590
Oh, no, it's not that serious...

00:01:06.170 --> 00:01:07.630
Are you in love or something?

00:01:10.630 --> 00:01:11.910
Bingo, eh?

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:19.680
Even the young squad leader who recaptured Vasel Bridge has troubles with the affairs of the heart?

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:21.440
Of course not!

00:01:21.440 --> 00:01:22.770
I'm not like you!

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:25.730
Come to think of it, your non-commissioned officer is a girl.

00:01:26.280 --> 00:01:29.200
I remember her name is Alicia or something.

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:37.720
Are you getting along well with her?

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:40.160
Somewhat.

00:01:40.160 --> 00:01:43.810
Seriously, this must be what you call "the grass is greener on the other side".

00:01:44.520 --> 00:01:49.510
Squad 1 is equipped with great warriors, but it lacks women.

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:50.930
I see.

00:01:52.220 --> 00:01:56.010
My mistake. I washed all the shirts.

00:01:56.600 --> 00:01:58.720
I'll lend you mine if you want.

00:01:58.720 --> 00:01:59.980
Are you all right with that?

00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:01.100
Thanks.

00:02:04.700 --> 00:02:06.520
Sir!

00:02:07.070 --> 00:02:09.730
You don't need to salute me here.

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:11.010
Y-Yes, sir!

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:12.480
Excuse me!

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.030
Your subordinate?

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:15.730
Yes.

00:02:15.730 --> 00:02:16.910
Let's go, Welkin.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:30.500
I hear Maximilian is returning after an absolute victory.

00:02:31.090 --> 00:02:32.310
That's good news.

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:34.250
Do we have the time to be happy?

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:37.880
Those Gallian dogs managed to take the Vasel Bridge from us.

00:02:37.880 --> 00:02:40.430
What the hell is the infantry doing?

00:02:40.430 --> 00:02:42.820
Hey, calm down.

00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:49.580
It was certainly a surprise, but their tactic of
crossing the river with a tank was interesting.

00:02:50.010 --> 00:02:53.020
The enemy sure has some funny tricks up their sleeves.

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:54.980
Funny, you say?

00:02:54.980 --> 00:02:56.500
How absurd.

00:02:56.500 --> 00:02:59.170
It's merely something a layman would think of.

00:02:59.170 --> 00:03:01.430
Our enemy is the lowly militia.

00:03:01.780 --> 00:03:04.420
I cannot believe we suffered a humiliating defeat at their hands.

00:03:04.920 --> 00:03:08.020
They have tarnished the authority of our Grace!

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:09.600
Yeah, yeah.

00:03:09.600 --> 00:03:14.010
If we could win by social status alone, this war would be much easier.

00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:17.800
This is not the time to be debating over such matters.

00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:24.340
The problem is that through this small revolt, the Gallian army is moving into a counterattack.

00:03:24.820 --> 00:03:26.510
Exactly.

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:28.600
Your Grace, Maximilian!

00:03:29.580 --> 00:03:31.310
We must remove it.

00:03:31.860 --> 00:03:37.890
Though it might be a small bud now, we must nip it before it becomes full-blown.

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:42.100
First, in order to push back the Gallian Army,

00:03:42.100 --> 00:03:46.440
we must increase our forces at the central front where resistance is strongest.

00:03:46.440 --> 00:03:51.710
To do this, we need to secure the supply route from Kloden in the southern part of Gallia.

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:53.630
Gregor.

00:03:53.630 --> 00:03:59.350
In order to restructure the central front, go defend Kloden as a base and take command of the front.

00:03:59.350 --> 00:04:00.340
Yes, sir!

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:06.180
Jaeger, I order you to support Gergor's unit from the back and also to maintain the supply route.

00:04:06.630 --> 00:04:08.070
Leave it to me.

00:04:08.460 --> 00:04:09.560
Selvaria.

00:04:09.560 --> 00:04:10.470
Yes!

00:04:11.020 --> 00:04:13.410
I am heading for Barious Desert.

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:15.550
You will accompany me.

00:04:15.550 --> 00:04:16.190
Understood.

00:04:16.740 --> 00:04:20.610
My life lies with your soul.

00:04:21.190 --> 00:04:24.370
Go! We shall eliminate the young buds of the Gallians.

00:04:25.040 --> 00:04:26.030
Yes!

00:04:27.420 --> 00:04:28.260
General Damon?

00:04:28.790 --> 00:04:30.390
Yeah. Do you know him?

00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:32.020
Know him?

00:04:32.020 --> 00:04:33.150
Let's see...

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:35.460
If we were rabbits running in the meadows,

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:38.290
he'd be the fox. That might be a good analogy.

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:40.140
You mean he's our natural enemy?

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:41.760
Absolutely.

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:46.230
Damon is nobility, as well as being a big shot in the Military.

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:47.890
Covering himself in authority,

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:50.220
he rushes in greedily to pounce upon his prey.

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:52.820
He's indeed a fox-like guy.

00:04:52.820 --> 00:04:55.400
Not only does he <i>not</i> consider us, the Militia, as comrades,

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:57.370
he doesn't even care about us.

00:04:58.350 --> 00:04:58.860
No!

00:04:59.410 --> 00:05:01.820
Foxes aren't greedy animals like that.

00:05:02.380 --> 00:05:03.380
That's true.

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:06.620
It would be insulting to foxes to be placed in the same category as that man.

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:09.100
So, what's going on with Damon?

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:16.140
Well, it seems that Squad 7 will have to assist the unit that Damon leads.

00:05:16.140 --> 00:05:17.520
Oh, here it is.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:19.800
Here, you can wear it.

00:05:20.480 --> 00:05:21.310
Thanks.

00:05:25.420 --> 00:05:26.680
Excuse me.

00:05:26.680 --> 00:05:28.190
Welkin...

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:38.770
I-I-I'm sorry!

00:05:39.320 --> 00:05:40.280
What's wrong?

00:05:40.280 --> 00:05:42.820
There's nothing to apologise for.

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:44.600
No, uh...

00:05:44.600 --> 00:05:45.390
Well...

00:05:45.390 --> 00:05:46.410
Oh.

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:53.290
The war god Ares wouldn't consider being humiliated by having his naked body seen by Aphrodite.

00:05:56.130 --> 00:06:02.340
To sum it up, I don't mind at all if you see my naked body.

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:04.160
But <i>I</i> mind!

00:06:04.160 --> 00:06:06.510
You're an assistant officer, right?

00:06:06.510 --> 00:06:12.020
If you are going to round up men, it's
high-time you get used to seeing them.

00:06:12.880 --> 00:06:14.810
Welkin, say something!

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:16.740
Make him wear some clothes, quick!

00:06:16.740 --> 00:06:19.030
She's right. You'll catch a cold.

00:06:19.030 --> 00:06:21.190
That's not the point!

00:06:21.740 --> 00:06:24.370
There. This will do, right?

00:06:24.370 --> 00:06:25.870
Sorry about that.

00:06:25.870 --> 00:06:28.650
Not at all, Captain Landzaat.

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:30.290
Just call me Faldio.

00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:31.540
Understood.

00:06:31.540 --> 00:06:32.910
Squad Leader Faldio.

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:36.910
This guy is <i>definitely</i> enjoying this...

00:06:36.910 --> 00:06:39.290
What's the matter, Alicia?

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:40.910
Oh, um...

00:06:40.910 --> 00:06:43.880
We've been summoned by General Damon of the Military.

00:06:44.430 --> 00:06:46.660
Oh, from General Damon?

00:06:49.280 --> 00:06:53.230
Squad 7 Leader, Lieutenant Welkin Gunther reporting.

00:06:53.230 --> 00:06:56.600
Assistant Officer, Sergeant Alicia Melchiott reporting.

00:06:56.600 --> 00:06:58.130
I see.

00:06:58.130 --> 00:07:00.840
So you are the son of General Gunther.

00:07:02.280 --> 00:07:03.590
You were looking for us?

00:07:03.590 --> 00:07:05.260
Huh? Oh.

00:07:05.260 --> 00:07:10.590
The reason I called you here is none other than to talk about the Kloden mission.

00:07:11.120 --> 00:07:17.000
Our Gallian Military is about to make an counterattack in the central front.

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:20.880
The key to that is this place... Kloden.

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:28.710
Currently located in this forest is the supply base for the Imperial Army, which is their basis for the central battle front.

00:07:29.260 --> 00:07:32.080
There's something like that in that forest?

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:35.050
That forest? You've been there before?

00:07:35.050 --> 00:07:38.270
Yeah. A couple of times for the university's extra curricular seminars.

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:41.010
Excuse me.

00:07:41.010 --> 00:07:46.250
This supply base can be considered the Imperial Army's lifeline for their central front.

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:49.490
If we cut off their supply route, the situation would favor us.

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:54.410
Therefore, we won't need you for this mission.

00:07:54.960 --> 00:07:55.650
What?

00:07:55.650 --> 00:07:56.990
What do you mean?

00:07:57.540 --> 00:07:58.940
Don't you get it?

00:07:58.940 --> 00:08:02.880
For such an important mission, you guys will just get in the way.

00:08:02.880 --> 00:08:07.890
But if you want to be our shields, then that's a different story.

00:08:11.660 --> 00:08:12.620
B-But...

00:08:12.620 --> 00:08:16.230
We were able to recapture Vasel Bridge with our own power!

00:08:16.230 --> 00:08:17.970
We won't get in the way!

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:20.620
What foolishness are you saying?

00:08:21.030 --> 00:08:23.360
That was nothing more than a stroke of luck.

00:08:23.360 --> 00:08:26.240
<i>I'm pissed! What wrong with him?</i>

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:28.880
<i>Hey, Welkin, say something!</i>

00:08:30.350 --> 00:08:34.200
No good. He's not listening at all.

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:35.680
I see.

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:37.610
If you want to participate that much,

00:08:37.610 --> 00:08:41.420
Sergeant, <i>you</i> may join the military if you want.

00:08:42.630 --> 00:08:44.790
I'll pass!

00:08:45.340 --> 00:08:46.740
I understand.

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:49.200
We won't participate in this mission.

00:08:49.960 --> 00:08:51.770
So then, excuse us.

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:53.480
Let's go, Alicia.

00:08:53.860 --> 00:08:55.340
Hey, wait!

00:08:59.120 --> 00:09:00.150
Damn.

00:09:00.520 --> 00:09:04.020
Hey, Welkin, don't you feel angry after being talked down to like that?

00:09:04.570 --> 00:09:05.800
Angry about what?

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:08.190
That old man kept making rude remarks.

00:09:08.700 --> 00:09:11.450
And he looks at me in a lewd way.

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:16.030
Besides, he summoned us to say we're unneeded; I'm sure he's making fun of us.

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:17.970
Talk back a little, will you?

00:09:17.970 --> 00:09:20.280
Talk back, you say...

00:09:20.830 --> 00:09:23.290
But anyway, didn't you see that room?

00:09:24.300 --> 00:09:28.950
It was filled with animal fur and ornaments that's used to make himself conspicious.

00:09:28.950 --> 00:09:30.630
I don't think I'll be able to become like that.

00:09:32.870 --> 00:09:35.970
That person says he doesn't need us.

00:09:35.970 --> 00:09:37.180
There's nothing wrong with that.

00:09:37.730 --> 00:09:41.680
Anyway, let's prepare so that we can sortie anytime.

00:09:49.450 --> 00:09:52.440
We welcome you, General Gregor.

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:57.650
We are glad to have you, who was feared in Fhirald as the Devil of the Empire.

00:09:57.650 --> 00:10:01.140
Now we can be assured of victory here in the Southern Front—

00:10:02.580 --> 00:10:04.170
Uh, well...

00:10:04.560 --> 00:10:06.740
And how is the war situation?

00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:08.210
Make it short.

00:10:08.210 --> 00:10:09.490
Y-Yes, sir.

00:10:09.490 --> 00:10:11.750
We have an equal number of troops on both sides.

00:10:11.750 --> 00:10:14.270
Skirmish battles are happening in limited places...

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:18.610
But there is nothing that would change the status quo of both armies.

00:10:18.610 --> 00:10:20.650
However, there's just one thing that requires your attention.

00:10:21.980 --> 00:10:29.590
We received information that a company led by General Damon will be launching an attack on us.

00:10:29.590 --> 00:10:30.810
Is that so.

00:10:30.810 --> 00:10:32.460
What do we do?

00:10:35.570 --> 00:10:37.000
Do not worry.

00:10:38.490 --> 00:10:39.950
What?!

00:10:40.410 --> 00:10:42.230
Don't participate in the mission?

00:10:42.230 --> 00:10:43.240
What the hell is that?

00:10:43.240 --> 00:10:45.080
We sure are looked down on.

00:10:45.080 --> 00:10:47.620
They don't consider us to be part of the fighting force.

00:10:47.620 --> 00:10:50.560
Damn! Those bastards from the Military!

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:52.700
I won't feel good until I go complain about it!

00:10:52.700 --> 00:10:53.340
Stop it.

00:10:54.220 --> 00:10:57.390
What now? You're ordering me?

00:10:57.390 --> 00:11:01.210
Yes. You promised to follow my orders, didn't you?

00:11:01.210 --> 00:11:04.130
Y-Yeah... Damn.

00:11:04.130 --> 00:11:05.810
Are you fine with that?

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:06.520
Huh?

00:11:06.980 --> 00:11:09.880
It's not like we <i>want</i> to fight, really.

00:11:09.880 --> 00:11:13.570
But we can't accept being humiliated like that all the time.

00:11:13.570 --> 00:11:14.310
That's right!

00:11:14.770 --> 00:11:19.580
We must make them recognise us, even if we have to use force!

00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:21.810
But, this is an order.

00:11:22.340 --> 00:11:23.760
An order, huh?

00:11:23.760 --> 00:11:25.090
That's what you say,

00:11:25.090 --> 00:11:27.080
but you just came back without making a single complaint, didn't you?

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:29.760
Isn't that why they look down on us?

00:11:30.300 --> 00:11:32.920
So... what should we do?

00:11:33.380 --> 00:11:34.990
Let me see...

00:11:36.050 --> 00:11:39.880
Do the cleaning and laundry at the living quarters then?

00:11:41.450 --> 00:11:42.770
Geez!

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:45.650
I can't keep up with you.

00:11:53.900 --> 00:11:58.740
We will now begin the operation of capturing the Kloden Forest supply base.

00:11:59.540 --> 00:12:01.160
All troops, charge!

00:12:06.250 --> 00:12:07.480
General Gregor!

00:12:07.480 --> 00:12:10.120
The Gallian army is invading from the south-west area of the base!

00:12:10.590 --> 00:12:11.650
They came.

00:12:11.650 --> 00:12:14.750
First, send a decoy unit right in front of them.

00:12:15.770 --> 00:12:18.050
They <i>should</i> take the bait.

00:12:18.510 --> 00:12:20.380
We will then crush them once they do so!

00:12:20.380 --> 00:12:21.400
B-But...

00:12:21.400 --> 00:12:24.170
If we do something like that, that unit will suffer severe casualties!

00:12:24.170 --> 00:12:25.010
It is inevitable.

00:12:25.480 --> 00:12:29.500
To exterminate the Gallians, we must resort to anything.

00:12:29.500 --> 00:12:30.720
I see...

00:12:31.190 --> 00:12:35.690
We will make them regret that they dare oppose our Empire!

00:12:39.570 --> 00:12:42.240
Damn. Why do we have to do this?

00:12:42.240 --> 00:12:45.570
This is a report of the last exercise.

00:12:45.570 --> 00:12:47.120
Please look over it.

00:12:47.600 --> 00:12:48.330
Sure.

00:12:48.330 --> 00:12:50.080
All right.

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:55.920
I'll hang these up. Susie, can you bring the ones we just washed?

00:12:55.920 --> 00:12:57.830
Yes, I got it.

00:12:58.930 --> 00:12:59.760
Sir?

00:12:59.760 --> 00:13:00.750
O-Oh.

00:13:01.210 --> 00:13:03.980
Leave it on my desk.

00:13:04.330 --> 00:13:05.590
Y-Yes, sir.

00:13:08.670 --> 00:13:10.900
Welkin doesn't make sense at all.

00:13:10.900 --> 00:13:13.410
Everyone's running helter-skelter and not acting as a unit.

00:13:13.410 --> 00:13:15.660
Why does this have to happen?

00:13:15.660 --> 00:13:17.960
I might not be able to deal with this in the future.

00:13:17.960 --> 00:13:19.910
What won't you be able to deal with?

00:13:19.910 --> 00:13:21.740
Like I said, Welkin...

00:13:24.900 --> 00:13:25.700
Hi.

00:13:27.190 --> 00:13:27.820
Hello.

00:13:28.290 --> 00:13:30.180
Shall I help you hang these up?

00:13:30.180 --> 00:13:32.000
No, thank you.

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:34.030
This is actually our mission.

00:13:34.030 --> 00:13:38.370
Looks like it's a season full of worries, whether it's for you or Welkin.

00:13:39.240 --> 00:13:40.980
I'll listen to your story if you want.

00:13:41.930 --> 00:13:43.140
No thanks.

00:13:47.980 --> 00:13:49.540
You forgot something.

00:13:49.540 --> 00:13:50.270
Oh.

00:14:02.930 --> 00:14:03.980
T-Thank you!

00:14:05.900 --> 00:14:08.810
<i>Honestly, what's with this guy?</i>

00:14:08.810 --> 00:14:10.960
You were thinking about Welkin, right?

00:14:11.460 --> 00:14:18.290
He's whimsical, hard-to-understand, and a
man who does everything his way, isn't he?

00:14:18.760 --> 00:14:19.720
That's right!

00:14:19.720 --> 00:14:22.920
He doesn't seem to mind the general's humiliating remarks.

00:14:22.920 --> 00:14:26.110
And he doesn't try to round up his subordinates at all.

00:14:26.110 --> 00:14:30.770
He's really whimsical and airheaded. And I really don't know what he's thinking. And he does everything his way!

00:14:30.770 --> 00:14:33.020
I feel like I'm always being led around by my nose.

00:14:33.020 --> 00:14:35.680
But you have the feeling that he will do anything for you guys.

00:14:36.150 --> 00:14:36.980
Am I wrong?

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:43.980
Like you said, he can't be understood by logic.

00:14:44.450 --> 00:14:47.910
But it's also true that he has more than just weak points.

00:14:48.500 --> 00:14:50.700
You can tell during the time when he recaptured Vasel Bridge.

00:14:51.160 --> 00:14:53.500
He's a man who does the job when he needs to.

00:14:53.500 --> 00:14:56.840
<i>It's the first time I saw him with this kind of expression.</i>

00:14:57.450 --> 00:15:00.790
Anyway, you need to believe in him.

00:15:01.260 --> 00:15:03.790
After all, you <i>are</i> his assistant officer.

00:15:26.660 --> 00:15:28.320
What in the world...

00:15:29.690 --> 00:15:31.250
Sir.

00:15:31.250 --> 00:15:34.030
65% of the Gallian Army has been devastated.

00:15:34.030 --> 00:15:36.200
They are beginning to retreat.

00:15:36.200 --> 00:15:41.050
We should let the injured soldiers return at once and reorganise our forces.

00:15:41.050 --> 00:15:42.170
You are too soft.

00:15:43.050 --> 00:15:46.340
How can you stop attacking when the enemy has his back turned toward you?

00:15:46.340 --> 00:15:46.800
Pursue them!

00:15:47.890 --> 00:15:49.650
But... that would put unneeded burden on the soldiers—

00:15:49.650 --> 00:15:50.460
I don't care.

00:15:51.180 --> 00:15:55.790
We do not need unpatriotic soldiers who cannot whip themselves to work for our Grace.

00:15:55.790 --> 00:16:02.740
We shall teach the dog who bit the lion that it will receive a proportionate amount of pain.

00:16:03.690 --> 00:16:07.940
<i>This is the true face of Gregor, a soldier feared as the Empire's Demon.</i>

00:16:08.410 --> 00:16:11.150
<i>He's absolutely cold-blooded.</i>

00:16:17.380 --> 00:16:18.440
H-Hey!

00:16:18.440 --> 00:16:19.860
Don't abandon your stations!

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:21.520
Don't run!

00:16:21.520 --> 00:16:22.400
General!

00:16:22.400 --> 00:16:24.410
Chase them. Reorganise the unit.

00:16:24.410 --> 00:16:26.540
Our army's casualty rate is over 70 percent!

00:16:27.020 --> 00:16:29.100
We can't continue fighting!

00:16:31.720 --> 00:16:35.890
After you have confirmed that I've retreated, give the retreat order to all troops.

00:16:36.640 --> 00:16:38.730
Hold out until then.

00:16:38.730 --> 00:16:39.350
Yes, sir.

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:42.240
But in the worst case scenario, my custody...

00:16:42.240 --> 00:16:44.520
Yeah, I understand.

00:16:48.350 --> 00:16:52.990
For the exchange of prisoners, I'll trade in their commanders.

00:16:52.990 --> 00:16:53.450
Yes, sir.

00:16:53.450 --> 00:16:54.520
Goodbye!

00:16:58.660 --> 00:16:59.950
Man your positions!

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:03.790
Fight until the last man stands!

00:17:04.990 --> 00:17:06.720
Annihilated?

00:17:06.720 --> 00:17:07.670
Yes.

00:17:07.670 --> 00:17:12.010
Only General Damon managed to escape, but it was a complete loss for the military.

00:17:13.090 --> 00:17:18.010
It was fortunate that Squad 7's participation was declined.

00:17:18.910 --> 00:17:20.220
However...

00:17:20.690 --> 00:17:26.400
We've received an order from headquarters for the Militia to head to Kloden Forest.

00:17:26.400 --> 00:17:28.310
The squad designated as the vanguard will be...

00:17:28.780 --> 00:17:30.940
...Squad 7.

00:17:32.740 --> 00:17:34.740
<i>No way...</i>

00:17:35.600 --> 00:17:36.870
<i>It's an impossible task.</i>

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:41.360
Our unit will depart for Kloden Forest tomorrow morning.

00:17:41.360 --> 00:17:43.290
Everyone is prepared, right?

00:17:45.790 --> 00:17:48.630
I understand what you're thinking.

00:17:49.090 --> 00:17:53.800
The Military, and moreover, the unit led by General Damon, was defeated.

00:17:54.200 --> 00:17:56.840
You're wondering whether or not it's possible for us in Squad 7.

00:17:57.950 --> 00:18:02.170
As I said before, I want you to do your utmost best to stay alive.

00:18:03.370 --> 00:18:07.250
So if you don't agree with this mission, tell me honestly.

00:18:09.290 --> 00:18:11.030
I don't have a choice, do I?

00:18:13.270 --> 00:18:14.510
I'll go along with the plan.

00:18:14.510 --> 00:18:17.040
Since we have to follow the squad leader's orders.

00:18:17.040 --> 00:18:18.410
You're right.

00:18:18.410 --> 00:18:20.410
It's the leader's order.

00:18:20.410 --> 00:18:23.710
And this is our chance to show the Military who's boss!

00:18:23.710 --> 00:18:24.330
Yes.

00:18:24.790 --> 00:18:26.030
I'll do it.

00:18:26.030 --> 00:18:27.450
I'll go too.

00:18:28.670 --> 00:18:29.710
M-Me too!

00:18:29.710 --> 00:18:30.160
Me too.

00:18:30.160 --> 00:18:31.440
Me too.

00:18:31.440 --> 00:18:33.170
Let's beat them!

00:18:33.640 --> 00:18:35.130
Thank you, everyone!

00:18:37.050 --> 00:18:38.900
Let us join in the fun too.

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:41.330
Faldio!

00:18:43.250 --> 00:18:44.390
What do you mean?

00:18:44.850 --> 00:18:48.940
We got permission from Captain Varrot to back you up.

00:18:50.110 --> 00:18:51.110
Really?

00:18:51.950 --> 00:18:53.940
Thank you, Faldio!

00:18:55.500 --> 00:18:59.110
We won't let you guys get all the attention, Welkin.

00:19:00.370 --> 00:19:02.160
All right, it's been decided!

00:19:02.660 --> 00:19:05.660
Let's do our best!

00:19:06.130 --> 00:19:07.100
Yeah!

00:19:08.590 --> 00:19:09.980
Thank you!

00:19:08.890 --> 00:19:10.710
What a strange man.

00:19:10.710 --> 00:19:12.150
Yeah, indeed.

00:19:12.150 --> 00:19:13.840
I'll leave it to you guys!

00:19:12.420 --> 00:19:15.630
But when we finally realised it, we were already taken in by him.

00:19:17.480 --> 00:19:19.470
See, I told you.

00:19:19.930 --> 00:19:22.430
He's a man that does things when he has to.

00:19:22.890 --> 00:19:23.520
Yes.

00:19:23.970 --> 00:19:27.220
I have a better opinion of you now.

00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:28.410
A better opinion?

00:19:28.870 --> 00:19:31.390
Why are you still talking like a stranger at a time like this?

00:19:31.870 --> 00:19:38.610
Our relationship is already at a stage where Ares showed his naked body, and Aphrodite, the veil that covers her body.

00:19:39.080 --> 00:19:40.820
Huh? What does that mean?

00:19:41.290 --> 00:19:45.180
It means we're already so close that we've shown each other our naked bodies and underwear.

00:19:46.460 --> 00:19:47.660
What?!

00:19:48.130 --> 00:19:49.250
Naked bodies and...

00:19:49.710 --> 00:19:50.710
Underwear?

00:19:52.030 --> 00:19:52.920
Right?

00:19:54.260 --> 00:19:55.320
You're the worst!

00:19:57.910 --> 00:19:59.140
Ouch!

00:19:59.640 --> 00:20:00.880
I-I'm sorry!

00:20:00.880 --> 00:20:02.810
Ouch...

00:20:03.350 --> 00:20:06.260
Geez. What are you doing?

00:20:06.730 --> 00:20:08.240
I-I'm sorry!

00:20:08.240 --> 00:20:09.890
Because Faldio said...

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:12.640
Hello, everyone.

00:20:12.640 --> 00:20:14.850
My name is Susie Evans.

00:20:14.850 --> 00:20:18.110
Although I joined the Militia with my father's strong recommendation,

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:21.010
I'm not good at combat or community life.

00:20:21.010 --> 00:20:25.850
But I will try hard to not taint the reputation of the Evans family.

00:20:25.850 --> 00:20:27.860
Nice to meet you all!

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:32.490
Next time on Valkyria Chronicles Chapter 5,

00:20:32.490 --> 00:20:34.500
Kloden`s Surprise Battle.

00:20:34.500 --> 00:20:37.290
The Evans family motto is Courage and Honesty.

00:20:34.990 --> 00:20:39.980
Chapter 5:

00:20:34.990 --> 00:20:39.980
Kloden`s Surprise Battle

00:20:37.290 --> 00:20:39.370
Susie Evans, reporting in!
